</div>

<<audio "SFX-bark" play>>
:: Day3_Dog {"position":"1075,500","size":"100,100"}
After that interaction, Em Ploughy’s head is pounding relentlessly. She rests her head on her hands for a moment, pressing her fingertips to her temples in an attempt to relieve the tension. Suddenly, Em Ploughy feels something cold against her leg. She looks down to find a dog touching her with its nose.

The dog shifts to its side, slightly lifting its leg in the air with what looks like a smile on his face. 

Em Ploughy coos, "Bandit, are you asking for a belly rub?" 

<div class = "choice">
[[ Pet the dog.->Day3_Dog_R1]]
[[ Ignore the dog and call Dahler Bill.->Day3_Dog_R2]]
</div>

:: Day3_Elder_R1-2 {}
Sue Ingyou was a challenging woman to please. On her t-shirt, Murphy the Moose proudly proclaimed his signature catchphrase “Believe in the magic of kindness!” Em Ploughy had a hard time imagining this woman held such a belief. 

“So you’re telling me,” the woman hissed, “That I pay thousands of dollars to come on this luxury cruise and I can’t even smoke inside?”  

Doing her best to keep the thousand watt smile in place, Em Ploughy said “We have designated smoking areas located throughout the ship in specific outdoor areas and select casino zones. I can print you a map if—”

“That’s why I came here! Before you interrupted me with all of that nonsense about smoking not being allowed, I was hoping to get some decent help, which seems to be in short supply,” Sue Ingyou reprimanded, eyeing Em Ploughy up and down. “There’s something wrong with the slot machine in the casino, it stole my money! You need to come fix it now or I’m going to file a complaint to your boss.” 

<div class = "choice">
[[Em Ploughy calls the casino staff for help, it isn’t her job to help with the slot machines.->Day3_End][$dailyBucket +=20]]
[[Em Ploughy doesn’t want to risk her job by saying no. She agrees to meet the old woman at the casino in an hour to take a look at the faulty slot machine.->Day3_Dog][$dailyBucket -=5]]
</div>

:: Day3_Elder_R1 {"position":"1050,250","size":"100,100"}
<<audio "SFX-smoking" play>>
<<if $bgLevel < 3 >>
  <<set $bgType = "stormy">>
  <<set $bgLevel += 1>>
<</if>>
“Ma’am, please put that cigarette out,” Em Ploughy chirped in what she hoped was a friendly and unthreatening tone, “This is a no smoking zone.” 

The old woman narrowed her eyes and took a deep inhale of her cigarette, blowing the smoke directly into Em Ploughy’s face as she pondered, “Is that so?”

With her jaw clenched, Em Ploughy takes a soothing breath and smiles as bright as the sun, just as the Executive Director advises all Guest Relations Agents to do when assisting passengers. 

The old woman, who had introduced herself to Em Ploughy as Sue Ingyou in a tone that made it clear her name was on the VIP (Very Indiscreet Purchaser) list, was disgruntled by many aspects of the cruise. She had let Em Ploughy know that she’d been standing at the desk waiting for her for the past 30 minutes. The view from her room isn't as scenic as in the brochure, the boat’s engines are too loud, they won’t let her smoke in the dining hall, the water isn’t blue enough, the salty air makes her joints hurt, there’s too many kids on the family-friendly themed cruise…

<div class = "choice">
[[Em Ploughy rolls her eyes discreetly.->Day3_Elder_R1-2]]
[[Em Ploughy smiles and nods sympathetically.->Day3_Elder_R1-2]]
</div>


:: Day3_Boss_R2 {"position":"1000,375","size":"100,100"}
"I knew you would agree, thank you! Such a team player! Maybe I’ll consider promoting you to be my third Executive Assistant. I really do need all the help I can get. Sometimes, it feels like I’m the only one that does anything around here. It truly is lonely at the top." With that, Dahler Bill walks out of the Guest Relations office.

<div class = "choice">
[[Em Ploughy tries to forget this encounter. ->Day3_Elder_R1]]
</div>

:: Day3_Boss_R1 {"position":"925,250","size":"100,100"}
<<set $bgType = "stormy">>
<<set $bgLevel = 1>>
"Why do you have to be such a downer? You’re just like this gloomy weather outside. You should lighten up a bit. This is a fun workplace, and many girls would be grateful to work here. I'll take care of it this time. But, in the meantime, you should rethink your attitude." With that, Dahler Bill walks out of the Guest Relations office.

<div class = "choice">
[[Em Ploughy tries to forget this encounter. ->Day3_Elder_R1]]
</div>

:: Day3_Start {"position":"1000,100","size":"100,100"}
<<audio "SFX-horn" play>>
<<set $bgType = "sunny">>
<<set $bgLevel = 1>>
Dahler Bill visits Em Ploughy at her desk before the guests start to wake up for the day to get breakfast. “I hate this weather, it really doesn’t work well with my suit. How do I look?”

Em Ploughy could not be any less interested in her boss’s wardrobe, but replies: “I think your suit looks lovely” in a sickly sweet tone. 

"You know, I don't really care what you think of me,” Dahler Bill retorts matter of factly, “Just make sure to do a good job, no, a SPECTACULAR job, and that everyone leaves with a smile on their face."

“Speaking of, could you take pictures of all the employees for our new ID badges? I think it would be a nice personal touch.”

<div class = "choice">
[[No.->Day3_Boss_R1][$dailyBucket +=20]]
[[Yes.->Day3_Boss_R2]]
</div>

