:: Day1_Dog_R2 {"position":"575,475","size":"100,100"}
Em Ploughy sits down and continues to work. The dog eventually settles down by her feet. By the time the owners come around asking for help, he has calmed down and is ready to go back with them. They are thankful that Em Ploughy caught their dog, and agree to put in a good word with Dahler Bill if she doesn’t report their beloved and well trained emotional support animal, Bandit.

<div class = "choice">
[[You've got a deal!->Day1_End]]
</div>

:: Day1_Dog_R1 {"position":"575,600","size":"100,100"}
The dog lets Em Ploughy pet him and reach for the leash. His eyes look drained, and he’s panting up a storm. She holds on tightly to the leash and waits until the owners start to catch up. Once they’re in her line of sight, she gestures towards the owners and hands over the pup. They are thankful that Em Ploughy caught their dog, and agree to put in a good word with Dahler Bill if she doesn’t report their beloved and well trained emotional support animal, Bandit.

<div class = "choice">
[[You've got a deal!->Day1_End]]
</div>

:: Day1_Dog {"position":"500,350","size":"100,100"}
<<audio "SFX-growl1" play>>
When Em Ploughy finally gets back to her desk, she throws herself into the comforting embrace of her trusty chair. There are parts of her body hurting that she didn't even know existed. Em Ploughy is massaging her sore legs when she hears shouting in the distance. She looks up to see a loose dog running with his leash in its mouth. 

“Since when are pets allowed on this cruise?” she wonders, then promptly decides she doesn’t have the energy to care. 

A couple is chasing after him while he runs in circles around them. He stops behind a chair and looks right at them. They're clearly out of breath, but they try to circle around the chair to secure him. Just before they're able to catch him, he jumps up and takes off once again. The couple shoot each other an annoyed look, take a deep breath, and start their chase anew.

As they slowly exit her view down the hallway, Em Ploughy goes back to her work. Shortly after, she looks up to see the dog quickly running towards her, no owner in sight. Startled, Em Ploughy stands up and the dog barres into her legs. He looks up at her with the leash in his mouth and drops it. 

<div class = "choice">
[[Try to get the leash and call his owners->Day1_Dog_R1]]
[[Ignore the situation and go back to work..->Day1_Dog_R2]]
</div>

:: Day1_Kid_R3 {"position":"400,550","size":"100,100"}
<<if $bgLevel < 3 >>
  <<set $bgType = "stormy">>
  <<set $bgLevel += 1>>
<</if>>

Em Ploughy remembers the stockpile of Murphy the Moose shaped lollipops hoarded in the bottom drawer of her desk and proclaims “Hello dolphin friend! If you swim back to my desk with me, I can give you a super special dolphin lollipop!”  

The child considers her offer, “Two lollipops.” 

Breathing out a sign of relief, Em Ploughy agrees.  

While taking the employee hallways back to the Guest Relations desk, they come to a fork in their path. The sign says “Security Office” with an arrow pointing left. Em Ploughy’s desk is to the right. She stared at the sign, exhausted, and wishing dearly to pass the child off to someone more qualified. 

<div class = "choice">
[[Go left and hope for their sakes that there's some candy in that office.->Day1_Dog][$dailyBucket +=10]]
[[Go right and get the child some candy before dropping him off. Em Ploughy needs to make sure that all guests have the most magical experience possible or there will be consequences.->Day1_Dog][$dailyBucket -=5]]
</div>

:: Day1_Kid_R2 {"position":"350,400","size":"100,100"}
<<audio "SFX-footstep-running" play>>
<<set $bgType = "stormy">>
<<set $bgLevel = 1>>
Muttering a word under her breath that would almost certainly get her written up, Em Ploughy took off after the child. 

For being no more than five years old, the child could run at an unbelievably fast pace, and for such a long time! He tore through hallway after hallway, up and down the stairwells, and across a mercifully empty VIP deck. He stayed far outside her grasp. Often, the only indicators that Em Ploughy was heading in the right direction were the rhythmic pitter patter of his slippered feet, fiendish giggles, and the occasional breathy declaration of “DOLPHIN POWER!” 

Upon reaching the top of the umpteenth stairwell, she closed her eyes and leaned forward to catch her breath. She leaned her sweat drenched forehead against the cool wall, contemplating what it said about her abilities as a Guest Relations Agent that a child was able to outrun and outsmart her. Huffing, puffing, and cursing the day dolphins were discovered, she decided to cut her losses and call security in shame back at the comfort of her desk. 

“Hi,” a voice breathes in her ear.

Em Ploughy jumped and let out an embarrassing squeak before finding herself looking down at the child in the shark onesie yet again. 

“Do you have any candy? Dolphins love candy, and candy is their favorite food.” 

<div class = "choice">
[[Em Ploughy has had enough! Screw this kid and his candy! Em Ploughy calls security and lets him be their problem->Day1_Dog][$dailyBucket +=10]]
[[Em Ploughy decides to get the dolphin some candy in order to avoid further upset. Guest Relations Agents have been fired for much less than an unhappy child!->Day1_Kid_R3][$dailyBucket -=5]]
</div>

:: Day1_Kid_R1-2 {}
She stood and straightened her uniform, then felt to ensure that her hair stayed put in its mandatory updo. It would be just her luck to get demerits for a crumpled skirt and crooked bun on the first day of the voyage.  

Glancing down at the child, she noticed his bright blue shark onesie. While keeping him in her peripheral, she scanned the near empty room. Her hopes that a mother, desperately searching for her feral child costumed as the king of the ocean, would run around the corner and solve this problem for her slowly depleted. 

This wasn’t the first time she had helped reunite a lost passenger with their family. All she needed to do was find out his information, then security could handle the rest. Attempting to project a reassuring aura, she gently smiled at the child, “Hey friend, it’s not safe to run around here so fast, someone could get hurt! Where are your parents?”

“I’m a dolphin.” He states from within his shark onesie as if it were the most obvious thing in the world. “Dolphins don’t have parents.” 
“Oh,” she paused, “then where did you run here from?”

“Dolphins don’t run, they swim,” he informed her.

Speaking through a smile of gritted teeth she asked, “Ok dolphin, where did you swim here from?”

Instantly the child was standing proudly on the counter bellowing “DOLPHIN POWER!” 

Before she could even blink, he was sprinting down the hallway at as fast as his legs could carry him

<div class = "choice">
[[Em Ploughy calls security and reports the missing child, they will know what to do next->Day1_End][$dailyBucket +=10]]
[[Em Ploughy chases after him! His antics could disrupt the other guests, or more importantly, get Em Ploughy in trouble!->Day1_Kid_R2][$dailyBucket -=5]]
</div>

:: Day1_Kid_R1 {"position":"300,250","size":"100,100"}
<<audio "SFX-announcement" play>>
The cruise was not off to a promising start. Em Ploughy slouched against her chair behind the guest relations desk, rubbing her eyes and sighing deeply as the family she just finished assisting walked away happily. It was truly astounding the number of issues that could be resolved by a complementary meet and greet with Murphy the Moose. 

Em Ploughy took a moment to center herself with a deep breath. It wouldn't do for a member of the esteemed Guest Relations team to be seen looking anything less than cheerful and enthusiastic to a nearly concerning degree. Sure, sitting behind a desk all day on a mega corporation’s themed cruise ship wasn’t her dream job, not by a long shot. But, at least she got to see the world! Even if it was just in fleeting glances stolen through the small window, she passed on her way to and from the crew quarters each day. 

Perched atop the shockingly comfortable adjustable office chair, her home away from home, Em Ploughy straightened her posture and pasted the company regulation smile across her face. She could do this! Whatever crazy request they hit her with next, she was prepared to handle herself with the poise and grace required of her position. 

“Oof!”

Suddenly Em Ploughy was rolling onto the cold hard linoleum floor, the wheels of her chair off the ground and spinning in the air. Sitting up, she starts, “What the he–”. Just inches in front of her face was that of a small child. With pink cheeks, a thin sheen of sweat across his forehead, and his chest rapidly expanding with obvious exertion, it wasn’t hard to figure out what, or who, sent her flying. His eyes widened as they met hers. 

“Good night!” he offered.
<div class = "choice">
[[“Good night?” she replied, checking her watch to verify that it was most certainly not past noon.->Day1_Kid_R1-2]]
[[“What?” She asks, “Did you hit your head when you catapulted into me?”->Day1_Kid_R1-2]] 
</div>



:: Day1_Start {"position":"250,100","size":"100,100"}
<<audio "SFX-horn" play>>
<<set $bgUsesLevel = true>>
<<set $bgType = "sunny">>
<<set $bgLevel = 1>>
Em Ploughy sits stiffly behind her new desk, waiting to meet her boss start her day as a Guest Relations Agent aboard the Great Dette.

“Oh, hello Em Ploughy, it’s lovely to finally meet you! I assume you’ve received our welcome letter, yes? Excellent! My name is Dahler Bill, the executive manager of this fine cruise ship. Isn’t she a beauty?” You’re lucky to be on board, we don’t accept just anyone, you know. Well, good luck today, you’ll need it! I was just kidding.. Or was I? Haha! Anyways, don’t mess this up or you’ll be hearing from me."

With that encouraging message out of the way, Dahler Bill turns to walk away and leaves Em to sit at her desk and await her first passenger...

<div class = "choice">
[[Got it!->Day1_Kid_R1]]
[[Nice to meet you too...->Day1_Kid_R1]]
</div>



:: Introduction {"position":"100,400","size":"100,100"}
<<audio "BG-waveSeagull" stop>>
<<audio "SFX-handwriting" play>>

<div class = "letter">
To our Newest Employee, 

Welcome aboard the Great Dette! 

We are delighted to have you join our cruise ship adventure as we sail across the Atlantic Ocean. As a member of the Guest Relations staff, you are a very important part of our team. We could not provide our passengers the most magical family-friendly experience of a lifetime in international waters without you! We kindly ask that you remember to treat all passengers with the utmost respect. It is your duty to help with any requests, no matter how big or small they may be. Failure to do so will likely result in your termination. 

We hope that you shine as bright as the sun, and don’t forget to smile!

Sincerely, 
Dahler Bill, Executive Manager
</div>

<div class = "main-button">
[[Start Day 1->Day1_Start]]
</div>

